const e={1138:{example:"China plays an important role in promoting Asian culture",extra:"cultural adj. 文化的。multicultural adj. 文化多样的"},1139:{example:"Western civilization was cradled in Ancient Greece 古希腊滋养了西方文明",extra:"cradle n./v. 摇篮，吊架，发源地/轻轻抱着 —— 这里翻译成了滋养。civilize=civilise v. 使文明，开化"},1140:{example:"The Renaissance was an epoch of unparalleled cultural achievement 文艺复兴时期是一个在文化上取得空前成就的时代",extra:"epoch n. （尤指出现新进步和大变革的）时代，纪元，时期——注意美音和英音的发音区别。unparalleled adj. 无双的，无比的，空前的"},1141:{example:"Their epic fight is the subject of a new film",extra:"他们的伟大战斗是一部新电影的主题"},1142:{example:"An obsolete ideology can hamper an economy",extra:"obsolete adj. 废弃的，过时的，老化的，淘汰的。hamper v./n. 阻碍，妨碍/带盖的方形大容器，食品盒，洗衣篮"},1143:{example:"Asia has a long tradition of tea drinking. China is of no exception",extra:"traditional adj. 传统的；惯例的。by tradition 根据传说；依照传说"},1144:{example:"The handshake is a social convention",extra:"conventional adj. 传统的；惯例的"},1145:{example:"The custom prevails over the whole area 该风俗盛行于这整个地区",extra:"prevail v. 占优势，占上风；流行，盛行（V for Vendetta 里元首的口头语 England Prevails-英格兰必胜）。 customs n. 海关；关税"},1146:{example:"Feudalism was not abolished in England util 1660",extra:"feudal adj. 封建的"},1147:{example:"They thought slavery was morally wrong",extra:"slave n. 奴隶"},1148:{example:"You can't divorce science from ethical questions",extra:"-"},1149:{example:"The old gentleman claimed himself to be a moral man, who had never told a lie in his life",extra:"immoral adj. 不道德的。moral principles 道德准则。moral standards 道德水准"},1150:{example:"The tribe's development was more primitive than that of their neighbours/neighbors",extra:"primitive adj. 早期的，原始的，远古的；简陋的"},1151:{example:"Many Aboriginals do not like the idea of a day to celebrate the British landing. 许多澳大利亚土著并不喜欢庆祝英国人登陆的日子",extra:"original adj. 原本的；最初的。origin n. 起源"},1152:{example:"The local inhabitants do not like the noisy tourists in summer",extra:"inhabit v. 居住于；栖息于"},1153:{example:"He is a native of Beijing",extra:"-"},1154:{example:"He provided local delicacies for his guests.他用当地的美味佳肴来招待客人",extra:"delicacy n. 美食，佳肴；慎重，周到；易碎，易损；精妙，精细"},1155:{example:"The exotic atmosphere will fascinate you",extra:"-"},1156:{example:"Some foreigners assimilate easily into our way of life",extra:"assimilate v. 加入，融入，同化；学习；吸收"},1157:{example:"I ran into an old friend in the alien land. 他乡遇故知",extra:"run into sb./sth. 偶然遇到、无意碰见（某人）/遇到、陷入（困境）；共计，合计。  alienate v. 使疏远；使不友好；离间。an alien culture 异域文化"},1158:{example:"The anthropologist contrasted two cultures in his lecture. 这位人类学家在讲座中将两种文化进行对比",extra:"contrast v./n. 对比，对照/差异，对照物，（屏幕、显示器）对比度。anthropology n. 人类学"},1159:{example:"Hepburn is known as a great humanitarian",extra:"-"},1160:{example:"They take great pride in their cultural heritage",extra:"-"},1161:{example:"He inherited a house from his father",extra:"inheritance n. 继承；遗产"},1162:{example:"He wears designer clothes and drives an antique car",extra:"designer clothes 名牌服装"},1163:{example:"Archaeology is the study of ancient civilizations",extra:"archaeological adj. 考古学的；archaeologist n. 考古学家"},1164:{example:"It took a long time to excavate the ancient city of Troy",extra:"excavation n. 挖掘；发掘"},1165:{example:"A visit to the museum is an unforgetable experience",extra:"-"},1166:{example:"Modern pottery is usually ornamental",extra:"ornamental /ˌɔː.nəˈmen.təl/ adj. 装饰性的，装饰用的。pot n. 壶，罐子"},1167:{example:"The jeweler will engrave the inside of the ring with her name",extra:"-"},1168:{example:"Using extremely different decorating schemes in adjoining rooms may result in lack of unity in style. 相邻的房间用悬殊太大的装修方案会导致风格不统一",extra:"adjoining adj. 相邻的。decoration n. 装饰，装饰品。decorative adj. 装饰性的。decorate A with B 用 B 装饰 A。"},1169:{example:"There are many religions in the world",extra:"religious adj. 宗教的"},1170:{example:"The scientists found that personal involvement in a ritual is necessary",extra:"-"},1171:{example:"He felt very sorry for his breach of etiquette. 他为他的失礼行为深感抱歉",extra:"breach n./v. 破坏，违反，不履行；（防御工事的）缺口/破坏，违反，不履行；（尤指从背后突袭）在...上打开缺口"},1172:{example:"His firmness in his belief supported him through difficulties",extra:"-"},1173:{example:"No words can express the secret agony of my soul. 没有语言能够表达我心灵的隐痛",extra:"agony n. （肉体或精神的）极度痛苦"},1174:{example:"We need a spirit of enterprise if we are to overcome our difficulties. 如果要克服困难，我们就要有进取心",extra:"enterprise n. 公司，组织，企业，计划，事业；事业心，进取心，创业精神，冒险精神。spiritual adj. 精神上的"},1175:{example:"This area was hollowed by sacred memories",extra:"-"},1176:{example:"The Ganges is hallowed as a sacred cleansing river",extra:"-"},1177:{example:"A holy person is spiritually pure",extra:"-"},1178:{example:"The election of a new pope is coming",extra:"-"},1179:{example:"I've heard a whisper that the bishop intends to leave. 我听到谣传说主教打算离开",extra:"-"},1180:{example:"The missionary was sent to India last year",extra:"-"},1181:{example:"The priest persuaded him to give up his bad habit",extra:"-"},1182:{example:"The Bible begins with the Genesis. 圣经的开篇是创世记",extra:"-"},1183:{example:"I'm just going to the church to see the priest",extra:"-"},1184:{example:"This cathedral was regarded as a miracle in architectual history",extra:"-"},1185:{example:"The choir sang the Amens beautifully. 唱诗班吟唱的“阿门”非常优美",extra:"choir 发音类似quiet去掉t的音"},1186:{example:"The man was a monk from Mount. MI",extra:"-"},1187:{example:"The temple has been considered an example of classic design",extra:"-"},1188:{example:"The pagoda perches on the top of the hill. 佛塔立在山顶上",extra:"perch v./n. 坐在...（的边缘）上，栖息于，停留于；使位于高处（或...的边缘）/河鲈；（鸟的）栖息处（尤指鸟笼里的细杆）；（常指能很好地俯视低处的）高座，高处"},1189:{example:"The empire had for years been falling into decadence",extra:"-"},1190:{example:"They made an objection to the imperial system with resolution. 他们坚决反对这种帝国制度",extra:"resolution n. 决议，正式决定；决心，决定；坚决；解决，消除；分辨率；分解"},1191:{example:"Britain has always had a large navy, called the Royal Navy",extra:"-"},1192:{example:"The Tang Dynasty is a period remarkable for its liberality",extra:"-"},1193:{example:"It seems that the paper has confused the chronology of these events",extra:"-"},1194:{example:"The emperor unified the country by the sword",extra:"-"},1195:{example:"The king is the most important person in a kingdom",extra:"-"},1196:{example:"They were bowing as the king and the queen walked in. 当国王和王后进来时，他们屈膝致敬",extra:"bow v./n. （使）鞠躬；（使）欠身；点头致意/弓"},1197:{example:"The prince fell in love with a fair young maiden",extra:"maiden 处女"},1198:{example:"The princess was ostracised for marrying a rich bourgeois man. 公主因与一位富有的资本家结婚而遭到排挤",extra:"ostracize=ostracise v. 故意避开；排挤，排斥。bourgeois  /ˈbɔːʒ.wɑː/ adj. 中产阶级的；追求物质享受的；平庸粗俗的"},1199:{example:"I enjoyed all the majesty of royal ceremonies",extra:"majestic adj. 宏伟的；庄严的"},1200:{example:"Virtue is the only true nobility. 万事不如美德高",extra:"virtue n. 美德，高山品德；优点，好处"},1201:{example:'The yound lord with the red gold hair bowed, "As you command, Lord Edword."',extra:"-"},1202:{example:"He was knighted for his war services",extra:"-"},1203:{example:"He became the legal guardian of his brother's daughter",extra:"guard n. 守卫 v. 保护"},1204:{example:"The soldiers were filled with nostalgia",extra:"-"},1205:{example:"My American friend tells me she is never as homesick as during this time of year around Thanksgiving",extra:"homesickness n. 思乡之情"},1206:{example:"Celebrity, money and possessions are too often the touchstones for teenagers. 名誉、金钱和财产常常成为青少年们衡量事物的标准",extra:"touchstone n. 试金石，检验标准"},1207:{example:"Being an engineer gives him a high status",extra:"social status 社会地位"},1208:{example:"He is a man with a special cultural background",extra:"-"},1209:{example:"It was a truly memorible experience",extra:"experienced adj. 经验丰富的"},1210:{example:"He preceded his lecture with a humorous anecdote.",extra:"precede v. （指时间或空间上）处在…之前，先于"},1211:{example:"His left knee was hurt in a traffic accident",extra:"accidental adj. 意外的；偶然的；附属的。by accident 偶然。 an aviation accident 空难"},1212:{example:"A serious incident along the border increased our fears of war",extra:"-"},1213:{example:"First thrive and then wive. 先立业，后成家",extra:"wive v. 娶妻"},1214:{example:"The empire was on the wane after its period of prosperity. 帝国在经历繁盛之后逐渐衰落",extra:"wane v. 衰减，减弱 on the ~ （权力、人气等）衰落，减弱。 prosper v. 成功；繁荣。prosperous adj. 繁荣的"},1215:{example:"This setback has drained away my keenness",extra:"drain sth. away （使）彻底消失;（使）流失。keenness n. 积极；敏锐，精明；渴望，热衷；锋利"},1216:{example:"Hardship disposes man to meet adversity. 困苦使人们愿意去客户困境",extra:"dispose sb. to/towards sb./sth. 表示使某人对某人或某事物产生一种倾向、态度或情感。"}};export{e as default};
